    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Import Libraries\n",
        "In this step, we import all the libraries needed for data handling, preprocessing, modeling, and evaluation."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aCMSSQUE56Gj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.svm import SVC\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VBCWZaUp59sx"
      },
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Load the Dataset\n",
        "Here we load the Pima Indians Diabetes dataset from the CSV file. The `Outcome` column is the target (1 = diabetes, 0 = no diabetes)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-E3_iNkz6VsC"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv('diabetes.csv')"
